# FastAPI Backend Rules

## Context
Python 3.12 + FastAPI + PostgreSQL. Routes live in app/routers/, business logic in
app/services/, database models in app/models/, Pydantic schemas in app/schemas/.
Alembic handles all schema migrations — never modify tables by hand.

## Architecture
- Use FastAPI's Depends() for dependency injection throughout.
- Service layer owns transactions; route handlers must not call session.commit() directly.
- Use SQLAlchemy 2.0 async sessions — all database calls must be awaited.
- Pydantic v2 models define every request/response boundary — never use raw dicts at the API layer.

## Style
- Always annotate every function parameter and return type.
- Use Ruff for linting and formatting (line length 100, enforced in CI).
- Use standard patterns for error handling across all services.
- Prefer async functions throughout; reserve sync functions for CPU-bound helpers only.
- Use Ruff for linting and formatting (line length 100, enforced in CI).

## Rules
- NEVER expose raw SQLAlchemy exceptions to API responses — catch and re-raise as HTTPException.
- NEVER log personally identifiable information (names, emails, IP addresses) at INFO level or above.
- ALWAYS include a docstring on every public service method describing inputs, outputs, and side effects.
- MUST run `mypy --strict` and `pytest` before pushing to any branch.
